From 99145eab1752d92c52a3fae3782ba7afe6df0b49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Oberlin <dmo.git@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:52:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] BD-J: do not initialize "present" applications when loading a
 title

Applications with control code PRESENT were init()ed as soon as the
title's BDJO was loaded, leaving their AppProxy in PAUSED state. They
are only listed in the applications database and should stay NOT_LOADED
until another application launches them.

This breaks discs where a launcher Xlet starts the real application
and first checks its state. Seen on "Bond 50th Anniversary" (Fox): the
autostart Xlet com.macrovision.bdplus.Handshake looks up the Xlet named
by its "-BD+XLET:" parameter and calls AppProxy.start() only if
getState() == NOT_LOADED; otherwise it gives up ("Application state
wasn't NOT_LOADED. Can't load it."), and the disc stays on a black
screen.

Leave the proxy of a PRESENT application untouched. AppProxy.start()
already loads and initializes a NOT_LOADED application.

Tested by starting 115 Blu-ray discs (95 of them with BD-J titles) to their
menu with VLC before and after the change; no disc regressed.
---
 src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/BDJLoader.java | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/BDJLoader.java b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/BDJLoader.java
index 2a126075..4b9cd254 100644
--- a/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/BDJLoader.java
+++ b/src/libbluray/bdj/java/org/videolan/BDJLoader.java
@@ -293,8 +293,11 @@ public class BDJLoader {
                     logger.info("Autostart xlet " + i + ": " + appTable[i].getInitialClass());
                     proxys[i].start();
                 } else if (code == AppEntry.PRESENT) {
-                    logger.info("Init xlet " + i + ": " + appTable[i].getInitialClass());
-                    proxys[i].init();
+                    /* "Present" applications are listed in the applications database but are not
+                     * loaded until something launches them. Leave the proxy in its current state
+                     * (NOT_LOADED for a new application): applications that launch another one
+                     * through AppProxy.start() may first check that it has not been loaded yet. */
+                    logger.info("Present xlet " + i + ": " + appTable[i].getInitialClass());
                 } else {
                     logger.info("Unsupported xlet code (" +code+") xlet " + i + ": " + appTable[i].getInitialClass());
                 }
